# ★ 저자·라이선스 모두 정해졌다(Min, Jeho · MIT). 남은 것은 저장소 공개 전환뿐이다
#   — docs/zenodo.md 4절.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these figures or this code, please cite both this work and the upstream data sources listed below."
title: "RadCalc — nuclide reference sheets and spectrum-solved shielding for radiation protection"
abstract: >-
  Reference sheets for 147 nuclides with half-life, decay mode, specific activity, photon, beta and
  alpha emission lines, and — for photon emitters — air kerma rate constants and half- and
  tenth-value layers solved across the whole emission spectrum rather than read from a single-energy
  table. The spectrum solution matters where a nuclide's dose rate is not dominated by one line:
  for Na-22 the lead half-value layer is 6.5 mm against the 10.5 mm implied by its strongest line,
  and for Sn-113 the tenth-value layer is 84 times the half-value layer rather than the 3.32 that
  holds for a single energy. Figures are narrow beam, with no buildup.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/aijhmin1031-eng/radiation-calc"
url: "https://radiation-lab.com/calc/nuclides/"
keywords:
  - health physics
  - radiation protection
  - gamma shielding
  - half-value layer
  - air kerma rate constant
  - nuclear decay data
  - bremsstrahlung
  - waste characterisation

